Now running a full Ethereum node—there aren’t many enterprise-grade SSDs with only a few TB, so you can’t really play. #ETH 
Why? Because of “state explosion”! Traditional blockchains are stuck in a rigid mindset: they insist on tightly stuffing every bad transaction from years past, along with every old account balance, into your local hard drive. This heavy-asset approach directly keeps ordinary players and regular servers out of the game. In the end, most nodes get fully managed in centralized data centers like Amazon AWS—turning decentralization into the biggest irony.
@NewtonProtocol  The team looked at its own compliance strategy library and took a different route. It decided not to have the node act as this “hard drive scapegoat”; instead, it chose to make the node purely “proletarian.”

